libopenwch-template — provenance and licensing
=============================================

What this repository is
-----------------------

The application skeleton for libopenwch: the two files a project needs before
it has any code of its own -- a `Makefile` and a `src/main.c` -- plus the editor
configuration for them.

It is deliberately not a collection of examples.  Worked programs for each
peripheral live in libopenwch-examples; a starting point that is also a demo is
a starting point you have to delete things from.

Two things are present as git submodules, untouched and unmodified, so updating
either is `git submodule update --remote` rather than a merge:

  libopenwch/           the library, and the only one the default build needs
  tools/wchlink/        libopenwch-tools' WCH-LinkE flasher, used only by
                        `make flash PROGRAMMER=wchlink`

